Tasks

1. Start your local MongoDB server and use the mongo shell to create a new database called instaAppData.

->  use instaAppData


2. Inside instaAppData, create a new user named 'playlistAdmin' with password 'music@123' and assign the 'dbAdmin' role — this user should be able to manage playlists and collections, but not read or write actual playlist data.

->  db.createUser({
        user: "playlistAdmin",
        pwd: "music@123",
        roles: [
            {
                role: "dbAdmin",
                db: "instaAppData"
            }
        ]
    })


3. Create another user in instaAppData named 'playlistViewer' with password 'view@123' and assign only the 'read' role — this user should only be able to view playlists, not modify or delete them.

->  db.createUser({
        user: "playlistViewer",
        pwd: "view@123",
        roles: [
            {
                role: "read",
                db: "instaAppData"
            }
        ]
    })


4. Test authentication by connecting to instaAppData as 'playlistViewer' and try to insert a new playlist document; note the error message and explain why it occurs.

->  mongosh --username playlistViewer --password "view@123" --authenticationDatabase instaAppData


5. Use the mongo shell to list all users and their roles in the instaAppData database, and explain in one line what each role allows the user to do.

->  db.getUsers()
->  {
        users: [
            {
                user: "playlistAdmin",
                roles: [
                    {
                        role: "dbAdmin",
                        db: "instaAppData"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                user: "playlistViewer",
                roles: [
                    {
                        role: "read",
                        db: "instaAppData"
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        ok: 1
    }

->  Role            |   Can do
->  dbAdmin         |   Manage database administration tasks, but not read/write actual data
->  read            |   Read/view database data but cannot insert, update, or delete